<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:17:33Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Femicide in Iran: When 'honor' becomes a death sentence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3395a6f7ae2eb314e43f152300bd809e9220b47361399978557772fa4a1da7b3</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:17:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/femicide-in-iran-when-honor-becomes-a-death-sentence/a-79681977--41194eafafb5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/femicide-in-iran-when-honor-becomes-a-death-sentence/a-79681977?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The murder of a young mother has once again sparked debate in Iran over so-called honor killings, the social acceptance of violence against women and the lack of protection for people vulnerable to gender-based violence.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India's young workers have a new colleague: AI</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fede12745ebe41f3f38043b6b4df2c7aa3bce4fedf04ab446cd035da9827ed30</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T11:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-young-workers-have-a-new-colleague-ai/a-79678342--60612fda0623.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-young-workers-have-a-new-colleague-ai/a-79678342?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Artificial intelligence is changing the way Indian workplaces operate — raising questions about productivity, skills and entry-level jobs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Wildfire kills 4 firefighters in Indonesia's Mount Bromo national park</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c934e198aa17963fe92627d98657f2b6c3ad66eae0f659983971f9967727da63</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T08:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wildfire-kills-4-firefighters-in-indonesia-s-mount-bromo-national-park/a-79676291--7fc8c1dafd75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wildfire-kills-4-firefighters-in-indonesia-s-mount-bromo-national-park/a-79676291?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The latest victims of Indonesia's wildfires were trapped by thick smoke and fast-spreading flames, authorities said. Meanwhile, the toxic haze from the fires has spread to Indonesia's neighbors.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India: CJP's Dipke detained amid call for fresh Delhi demo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d9729c7d181d1e267741340b564a019cc2734d9422e849cb157c5dd06bf602d</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T06:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-cjp-s-dipke-detained-amid-call-for-fresh-delhi-demo/live-79675849--c55ce4c4fba8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-cjp-s-dipke-detained-amid-call-for-fresh-delhi-demo/live-79675849?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police placed the founder of the Cockroach Janta Party, Abhijeet Dipke, in preventive detention. He was calling for a protest in central Delhi in defiance of police efforts to restrict it.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India faces water and power shortages after weak monsoon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f547f8791b1d1018463d56a90efd9b4239bf38826a14bbfb242f057f211f28dc</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-shortages-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540--3ab74afcb33c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-shortages-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A weak monsoon in India is hitting farmers, water supplies and the power system, while raising wider questions about increasingly erratic rainfall and the economic costs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea warns of AI-aided hacking after bank data breaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec0425816692f33c7a0a7519e05a1b190bae9f131963cc8a7093a63f608bc804</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T12:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922--3290ee11faa1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seoul is alarmed after a recent breach of South Korean banks' cyber defenses that reportedly involved AI-assisted hacking. Officials warn such methods could be used to also target other sectors and government agencies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>A brutal assault reignites fears over women's safety in India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe7f6cb5bce7aa02fc3277cd12dcece65f8de19777b343b0a9a88a31a7bc8a45</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T17:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-brutal-assault-reignites-fears-over-women-s-safety-in-india/a-79501471--bceecddefb45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-brutal-assault-reignites-fears-over-women-s-safety-in-india/a-79501471?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A string of sexual violence cases has revived questions about women's safety in India, fueling fear, protests and demands for action.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Lawyer of Junaid Hafeez, a Pakistai scholar imprisoned for 13 years, is hopeful for his release</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec738f833b1fd8d2a5c5a937420b44296756c09e9a3650d95343aee5a0bdb032</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-pakistai-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207--6c93b577eab6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-pakistai-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A former Fulbright scholar, Junaid Hafeez was sentenced to death under Pakistan's controversial blasphemy laws. His family and lawyer told DW there is now hope a court will overturn the conviction.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea has recently completed two road bridges easing transport to strategic allies Russia and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32b6364eb60b241f4a1c766784daed2445f33576d15b276e8ac8ec1b69d3ac36</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-has-recently-completed-two-road-bridges-easing-transport-to-strategic-allies-russia-and-/a-79473981--09998bc65869.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-has-recently-completed-two-road-bridges-easing-transport-to-strategic-allies-russia-and-china/a-79473981?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two recently opened bridges are expected to ease trade and transport between North Korea and its powerful neighbors. The new connections come as Pyongyang builds strategic ties with China and Russia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48601a0841cb6a0ed9185cbeccf6bcf0351c2e8e14ea6f0e8014f4319fa9e430</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
